---
import ToolLayout from '../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
---

<ToolLayout
	title="About — MeetingPlannerTimeZone"
	description="MeetingPlannerTimeZone is a free set of time zone tools for finding the best time to meet or call across the world — no sign-up required."
>
	<section class="hero-mesh border-b border-hairline bg-canvas px-6 py-16">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
			<p class="text-mono-eyebrow uppercase text-mute">About</p>
			<h1 class="mt-2 text-display-xl text-ink">Time zone math, without the headache</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-body-lg text-body">
				MeetingPlannerTimeZone is a small collection of free tools for figuring out when to meet or call
				someone in another part of the world.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-24 pt-16">
		<div class="flex flex-col gap-8">
			<div>
				<h2 class="text-heading-md text-ink">Why this exists</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-lg text-body">
					Scheduling across time zones is a small problem, but it's an annoying one — juggling UTC offsets,
					daylight saving changes, and "wait, is that AM or PM their time?" shouldn't take longer than the
					meeting itself. This site brings the tools we kept reaching for into one place: a multi-city
					meeting planner, a two-city calculator, a timezone converter, and a world clock.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-heading-md text-ink">How it works</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-lg text-body">
					Every calculation runs directly in your browser. There's no account to create and no server
					processing your schedule — pick your cities, and the tool does the conversion instantly. When you
					share a link, the details are encoded in the URL itself so the person on the other end sees the
					same result you do.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<h2 class="text-heading-md text-ink">Feedback</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-lg text-body">
					Found a bug, or have an idea for a tool that would help? <a
						href="/contact"
						class="text-link hover:text-link-deep">Get in touch</a
					> — we'd like to hear about it.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</ToolLayout>
